  "skeleton": "a hollow fallen log lying on its side, its open end to the left: root under the middle of its underside; tip at the bottom of the open end's rim and tipR at the bottom of the far (right) end (it rocks on one or the other); body (the log with its moss) on them; the little fern on its own bones at its foot in the log's top (fernL and fernR, the left and right fronds, layered behind the log so their feet tuck under its top edge). The log never moves by itself: only a bump, wind or something landing on it moves it.",
